## Phase 5a acceptance probe — Quartz scheduler `go fn()` on Windows.
##
## Spawns a worker task that prints, then `await`s it from main.
## End-to-end this exercises:
##  - sched_init (pthread_mutex_init + pthread_cond_init shims; allocations)
##  - worker thread spawn (pthread_create → CreateThread)
##  - task enqueue + dequeue (CONDITION_VARIABLE + SRWLOCK shims)
##  - sched_park / sched_wake (await waits, worker re-enqueues)
##  - pthread_join shutdown path (WaitForSingleObject + CloseHandle)
##
## On native macOS/Linux: prints
##     worker: started
##     worker: done
##     main: joined
## On Windows .exe (mechanical link verification + runtime if Windows host available):
## same expected output. No I/O, no sleep, no timers — pure-compute path
## that touches only the threading/sync primitives now backed by Win32.

def worker(): Int
  puts("worker: started")
  puts("worker: done")
  return 0
end

def main(): Int
  var w = go worker()
  await w
  puts("main: joined")
  return 0
end
